35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, transport costs are huge when we go far! Also, whole-building lets are risky because if someone cancels, the rest of us have to pay for them. That's not fair at all!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It seems that staying together in one place is the key to helping our members bond. However, I was saddened to see that some members stop coming to the club entirely after missing a camp.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The workload for public bookings is excessive, with a complex lottery and rigid application process. Additionally, staying on campus means we must cook for ourselves, which takes hours away from training.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,"The inland places sound like a nightmare! Eight people to a room and strict lights out? And our own hall is way too crowded, so we'd have to train at weird hours. We need something better!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"Public beds are quite affordable, but I've found that a third of our members can't even reach campus by 9 AM without paying for a room. We need to consider these hidden costs.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"If we go far, the transport costs will be huge, and those non-refundable deposits for whole buildings sound like a total headache. Maybe staying closer or using public facilities is safer for our wallets?","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"If we want to prevent members from drifting away, we must ensure the environment encourages them to mingle. A place where we all sleep under one roof seems most promising.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Given the administrative burden of public bookings and the time lost to cooking on campus, we should avoid those options. We need a destination that doesn't exhaust the organizers before the camp even begins.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"I don't want to be tired or train at midnight! If the inland places are too crowded and the hall is too busy, we should look for somewhere we can actually relax and sleep properly.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"If we stay on campus, we'll have to pay for rooms for a third of the members anyway. When we add that to the other costs, the ""cheaper"" local option might not be so cheap.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"It sounds like every option has a catch! If we go far, transport is expensive. If we stay local, some people still need beds. We need a balance that doesn't punish anyone financially.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"It is heartbreaking to think that some may leave the club because they feel isolated. We must prioritize a place where everyone stays together, as that is how the seniors say we truly bond.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"If we avoid the administrative nightmare of public centers and the labor of campus cooking, a private lodge seems the most reasonable, provided we can manage the financial risks Mio mentioned.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,"I agree with Ryuji! If the other places are too crowded or make us train at weird times, a lodge sounds way better. As long as we can actually sleep, I'm for it!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"A lodge might be comfortable, but non-refundable deposits and high transport costs are risky. We must be certain about the final budget before we commit to an expensive or rigid payment plan.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I'm really worried about those non-refundable deposits. If someone drops out, it's not fair for the rest of us to pay. But if the other options are too crowded or stressful, what's left?","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"Perhaps we can find a way to manage the deposits together. If staying in one place is the only way to keep our members from drifting apart, it is a risk worth taking.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,The administrative burden of public centers and the labor of campus cooking are simply too high. A lodge is the only option that protects the organizers' time and ensures quality training.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Rin,,I'm with Ryuji! I can't stand the idea of eight people in one room or training at midnight. A lodge sounds like the only place we can actually get some real rest!,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"I understand the desire for comfort and bonding, but we cannot ignore the financial risks. Between high transport costs and rigid deposits, a lodge could easily lead to another budget deficit.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
